import ../../ui/application.dl
import interface.dl
import workspace.dl

to close the ribbon application {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set instance to view's instance
    set state to instance's state as a pointer to ribbon demo state
    close view
    close instance
    destroy the value at view
    deallocate view
    destroy the value at instance
    deallocate instance
    deallocate state

function open the ribbon using {a pointer to UI driver:driver}:
    globals:
        ribbon studio
    execute:
        set state to storage for one slot initialized with (a new ribbon demo state)
        set instance to storage for one slot initialized with (an instance of ribbon studio with state state)
        bind (the control labeled "Editor" in instance) in instance to (the function named "paint the ribbon workspace on $") for event 1
        set view to storage for one slot initialized with (a UI view of instance sized 1280 by 800 using fonts "assets/fonts/NotoSans-Regular.ttf" and "assets/fonts/NotoSans-SemiBold.ttf" with driver)
        set state's view to view
        set view's close action to (the function named "close the ribbon application $") as a pointer
        run view
